			"url": "https://github.com/denoland/deno/issues/5432",
			"summary": "A long-time core collaborator (not a committer) explains how Deno compiles TypeScript, why startup costs about ten times more than JavaScript, and lays out an ordered, evolutionary plan: move dependency analysis to Rust, add a no-check type-stripping mode, profile tsc, try parsing in Rust and feeding tsc a serialised AST, optimise tsc for V8, and only last, if ever, port type checking to Rust, which he doubts would pay off.",
			"actorId": 1282577,
			"actorType": "human"
		},
